course: dictionary
lesson: 5602
title: A boat that saves lives
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lifeboat is a boat that helps people in trouble on the water. Some lifeboats wait on the coast, ready to rush out and rescue swimmers and sailors caught in a storm. Others are small boats carried on a big ship, so people can escape if the ship sinks.
explain: Look at the two parts of the word: life and boat. A lifeboat is a boat that saves lives. When you meet lifeboat, read the words around it. The lifeboat crew, the lifeboat station and the lifeboat drill tell you it is a boat for rescue.
explain: «In the lifeboat dilemma there is room for only some people.» Here the lifeboat is a picture of a hard choice. A dilemma is a choice where every option costs something, so you must think about which way of choosing is fair.
fact: A lifeboat is a strong boat kept on the coast, for rescuing people in danger at sea.
fact: A lifeboat can also be a small boat carried on a ship, used to escape if the ship sinks.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, the RNLI runs lifeboats, and many of the crew are volunteers.
fact: «Lifeboat drill» means practising what to do if a ship is in danger.
fact: The Titanic story is famous because there were not enough lifeboats for everyone on board.
exercise: What is a lifeboat? | A type of fish that lives in deep water | A boat for racing on a lake | A large boat that carries cars across a river | *A strong boat kept on the coast to rescue people in danger at sea
exercise: «In the lifeboat dilemma there is room for only some people.» What does dilemma mean here? | A type of sail | *A hard choice where every option costs something | A fun game played on a boat | A very fast journey
exercise: Which phrase means the base where a lifeboat is kept? | lifeboat drill | lifeboat crew | *lifeboat station | lifeboat dilemma
test: On a ship, what is a small lifeboat for? | To catch fish in deep water | To race other ships | *To help people escape if the ship sinks | To carry cargo across the ocean
test: Why is the Titanic story famous for lifeboats? | Because it had a lifeboat made of gold | *Because there were not enough lifeboats for everyone | Because the ship was the fastest ever built | Because it sank in a river
exam: Which word means a boat that saves lives at sea? | harbour | seaweed | *lifeboat | lifejacket
